 "_doc_work_bp": "Per-node work multipliers (design chapter 39, section 1.6) are calibrated to the completion targets: with the late research capacity these seats build (slice 6c), half of the design's surcharge above 10,000.",
 "_doc_critical_relief": "Job 4b (design chapter 39, section 8.5, items 1-3): the victory-critical nodes of tiers 7-9 take less work (tier 7 at 50%, tier 8 at 35%, tier 9 at 30%: section 2.7's rule, work = 36 months of the median seat's capacity in the class, applied to the advanced and frontier research the native seats actually build, one or two high-energy laboratories), their leads come at half the evidence (tier 7) or 40% of it (tiers 8-9), and the serial jump nodes T162-T167 have 30 minimum months instead of 36. Breadth costs, family locks and exclusive groups are unchanged.",
 "_doc_ruleset_3_1": "Ruleset 3.1 calibration: with public schooling the works of every seat are staffed, so practice evidence and research run faster from the Middle Ages on. Against ruleset 3.0 the pacing eras from medieval to scientific_method take 1.25x the evidence, tiers 4-6 1.6x the evidence and 1.5x the work, tiers 7-9 1.3x and 1.0x. Nodes of the merged graph (scripts/merge_late_tech.py) were removed from 'nodes'."
}
